<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka T-bill yields rise at weekly auction.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka T-bill yields rise at weekly auction.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yields of three-, six- and 12-month Sri Lankan treasury bills rose at Wednesday's auction with three- and twelve-month maturities oversubscribed, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>		  bids received   bids accepted   avg yield</p>
<p>    3 months     3,517	     2,806	  17.42 (17.27)</p>
<p>    6 months	 100		  85	  17.48 (17.26)</p>
<p>   12 months     1,682	     1,404	  17.52 (17.40)</p>
<p>The bank said it purchased bills totalling 326 million rupees. NOTE - Bids in million rupees, yields in percent (previous week's yields in brackets).</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom 434319</p>
</text>
